WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.465
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:05.450
MAYA KACZOROWSKI: Hi,
I'm Maya Kaczorowski,

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.119
and I'm here at KubeCon
EU in Copenhagen

00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:09.540
walking the show floor.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.990
And here with JFrog.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:11.760
Hi.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.490
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN: Hi, I'm Raj.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.340
I'm with JFrog and I take
care of technology alliances

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.150
and partnerships, and I take
care of the Google partnership

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.129
for the last year or so.

00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:23.420
MAYA KACZOROWSKI: That's great.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.730
Raj, how does JFrog
work with GKE?

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:29.780
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN: So we have
been very closely tied with GKE

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.410
and we have all of our
instances running on GKE.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:38.120
Our Artifactory is provided
as a product on GKE.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.580
And we also are providing
the Kubernetes registry now

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:48.049
as part of our contribution
to the community.

00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:50.090
And this is something
which we have been involved

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.020
in the last couple of years as
part of the development of many

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:57.110
of the Kubernetes registry
as a de facto registry

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.819
for implementing
Kubernetes clusters.

00:00:58.819 --> 00:01:00.110
MAYA KACZOROWSKI: That's great.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:03.770
So if a customer wants to use
JFrog, it's super easy for them

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:04.519
to go find it.

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:05.720
And what they do?

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.970
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN: Absolutely.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:11.090
It's basically available
on GCP as a SAS offering.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.172
And we also support
the Grafeas platform.

00:01:16.172 --> 00:01:17.630
And that is the
most important part

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.222
because our products
are Grafeas API,

00:01:20.222 --> 00:01:23.990
and the Xray product
has a Grafeas API

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:28.070
which works seamlessly
with the Grafeas platform.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:33.440
And we also are very closely
working with Orbitera.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.500
This is our test platform.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:39.100
If anybody wants to take a
test drive on JFrog products--

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:39.560
MAYA KACZOROWSKI:
They can use Orbitera.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.268
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN:
They can use Orbitera,

00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:44.670
and we provide a free
instance on Orbitera,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.430
which there is a set up there
where people can go in and play

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:52.979
with JFrog products and also
experience how GCP works.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.020
MAYA KACZOROWSKI: Got it.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.840
So if I want to test it
out, go check out Orbitera?

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:56.726
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN: Yes.

00:01:56.726 --> 00:01:58.340
MAYA KACZOROWSKI: Anything else
about the Google partnership

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.050
with JFrog you want to touch on?

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.050
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN: Yeah.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.470
I mean Google is one of
our premier partners,

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.810
and we have been
working very closely

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:11.210
on Grafeas, on Kubernetes
as a contributor,

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.410
and also now Helm repository.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:16.650
So Helm is something which we
have been using very closely.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.272
And that is now
available on GCP as well.

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:21.980
MAYA KACZOROWSKI:
Thank you so much, Raj.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:22.160
RAJ PANCHAPAKESAN: All right.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:22.520
Thank you.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:23.590
MAYA KACZOROWSKI: Thanks.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.994
And thanks, all, for
joining us keep KubeCon EU.

00:02:25.994 --> 00:02:26.660
Have a good one.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:30.010
[MUSIC PLAYING]

